# After `$isPrototypeChainPlain` returns true, the library's own source omits lookups at an allocation.
# The result reads bytes that the runtime maintains. The walk has no operation there for a run-time check to test.
# With testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime the true result is checked against the objects themselves, for each queried class.
# The check reads the class object's own `prototype`, without reifying it, and follows each link above it in step with the records of the classes, which are the tables that arm the bytes.
# Each object must be the prototype object of the record's class, and the last one must be directly below Object.prototype. The properties on those objects are not checked.
# RUN(FORM): walk f4 mechanisms=all testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime
# FORM: [[yes]]: boolean @Boolean = AreMembersUnchanged
# FORM: AskObjectAgain {{*}}, -, [[yes]] key="prototype" function=f2 [asksChainAbovePrototype]
# FORM: AskObjectAgain {{*}}, -, [[yes]] key="prototype" function=f3 [asksChainAbovePrototype]
# With nothing changed, and with the changes that the promise allows, nothing crashes.
# RUN(QUIET): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime keep = x => x; born = () => true; early = function () { }; later = function () { };
# QUIET: yes yes
# QUIET-NEXT: yes yes
# QUIET-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(STORED): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime keep = x => x; born = () => true; early = function () { }; later = function (Meter, Base) { Meter.prototype.other = function () { }; Base.prototype.more = 1; Base.prototype.reach = function () { return "wrapped"; }; };
# STORED: yes yes
# STORED-NEXT: yes yes
# STORED-NEXT: exited with 0
# A link that changes makes the result false, and the run-time check does not run.
# RUN(LINK): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime keep = x => x; born = () => true; early = function () { }; later = function (Meter, Base) { Object.setPrototypeOf(Meter.prototype, { }); };
# LINK: yes yes
# LINK-NEXT: no no
# LINK-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(ABOVE): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime keep = x => x; born = () => true; early = function () { }; later = function (Meter, Base) { Object.setPrototypeOf(Base.prototype, { }); };
# ABOVE: yes yes
# ABOVE-NEXT: no no
# ABOVE-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(REPLACED): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime keep = x => x; born = () => true; early = function () { }; later = function (Meter, Base, Other) { Other.prototype = { }; };
# REPLACED: yes yes
# REPLACED-NEXT: no no
# REPLACED-NEXT: exited with 0
# Fault injection, testing=AssumeGuardsAndFacts: the test is folded to true at compile time. The guards are still started before it.
# With the fault injected, the run-time check stays silent on an unchanged program.
# RUN(LIEQUIET): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime,AssumeGuardsAndFacts keep = x => x; born = () => true; early = function () { }; later = function () { };
# LIEQUIET: yes yes
# LIEQUIET-NEXT: yes yes
# LIEQUIET-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(LIELINK): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime,AssumeGuardsAndFacts keep = x => x; born = () => true; early = function () { }; later = function (Meter, Base) { Object.setPrototypeOf(Meter.prototype, { }); };
# LIELINK: yes yes
# LIELINK-NEXT: bun: internal AOT error: property lookup check failed
# LIELINK-NEXT: the check that the prototype chain of a class is unchanged passed, but a link above the prototype of the class has changed
# LIELINK: crashed with
# RUN(LIEABOVE): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime,AssumeGuardsAndFacts keep = x => x; born = () => true; early = function () { }; later = function (Meter, Base) { Object.setPrototypeOf(Base.prototype, { }); };
# LIEABOVE: yes yes
# LIEABOVE-NEXT: bun: internal AOT error: property lookup check failed
# LIEABOVE-NEXT: the check that the prototype chain of a class is unchanged passed, but a link above the prototype of the class has changed
# LIEABOVE: crashed with
# Every object on the chain is still a holder that the tables know, but one holder is skipped. A traversal that only tested "is this a known holder" would accept the chain.
# RUN(LIESKIPS): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime,AssumeGuardsAndFacts keep = x => x; born = () => true; early = function () { }; later = function (Meter, Base) { Object.setPrototypeOf(Meter.prototype, Object.prototype); };
# LIESKIPS: yes yes
# LIESKIPS-NEXT: bun: internal AOT error: property lookup check failed
# LIESKIPS-NEXT: the check that the prototype chain of a class is unchanged passed, but a link above the prototype of the class has changed
# LIESKIPS: crashed with
# RUN(LIEREPLACED): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime,AssumeGuardsAndFacts keep = x => x; born = () => true; early = function () { }; later = function (Meter, Base, Other) { Other.prototype = { }; };
# LIEREPLACED: yes yes
# LIEREPLACED-NEXT: bun: internal AOT error: property lookup check failed
# LIEREPLACED-NEXT: the check that the prototype chain of a class is unchanged passed, but the prototype of the class was replaced
